# The published CLI bin MUST have LF line endings. A CRLF shebang
# (`#!/usr/bin/env node\r`) breaks `npx` on macOS/Linux ("env: node\r: No such
# file or directory") and mangles the Windows cmd-shim, producing
# "Cannot find module" / "'…' is not recognized as an internal or external
# command". Forcing eol=lf here means git checks these out as LF on every OS, so
# `npm publish` from any machine packs LF.
cli/bin/vibekit.mjs   text eol=lf
cli/src/**            text eol=lf
cli/scripts/**        text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF to be executable.
*.sh                  text eol=lf
